Stage 3: SELECT PLAYER list-dialog INTERACTIONS -- row-select (red bar moves), OK/CANCEL button
activate, and the event-queue / dirty-repaint fixes that make dialog-internal clicks work.

Clicking a dialog element (row / OK / CANCEL / arrow) now recurses the hit-test into the dialog's
child elements and dispatches their [elem+0x4660] activate methods faithfully.  All asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.  Fixes (root causes):

 - FUN_1000_3566 + FUN_0000_1eb4 (hit-test): the LEAVE (0x200) / ENTER (0x400) synthesized event
   records are written into the QUEUE NODE that 3566 allocates (asm returns it in BX), NOT into the
   old hover element.  The patch-128 `oldfe0c` write clobbered a dialog CONTAINER node's word0 (cls=4
   -> 0x400), so the hit-test never recursed into the container's buttons/rows.  3566 publishes BX in
   the shim global g_fist_ev_node; the hit-test writes the event fields there.

 - FUN_0000_cf6b (OK/CANCEL activate): base-lost result store rebased to the DGROUP model
   (a85d = low byte of word[base + word[elem+2] + 1]); cc33 exits on a85d != 0xff.

 - FUN_0000_ccde (list-row activate): coord read rebased -- si = the drained event node
   word[DGROUP:0x18e2] (Ghidra bound it to param_3=base); row = byteTab[0xe88f + ((clickY-y0)>>1)]
   + scroll-top; on change: a838 = row, d066() marks the list dirty.

 - FUN_0000_cc33 (modal loop EXIT): the button-click exit rebuild `1cdb` had a dropped saved handle
   (`unaff_CS` garbage) + scrambled arg order -> wild deref.  Mirror the init call with ax := iVar1;
   set CF = (a85d >= 2) (CANCEL >= 2 -> menu, OK < 2 -> proceed).

 - FUN_0000_20d6 / FUN_0000_2043: the container PAINT / FORWARD-paint child-setup walkers (fall into
   20ea / 2057) were base-lost host-pointer derefs -> SIGSEGV on the dialog exit repaint.  Rebased to
   the DGROUP model, reusing the already-correct 20ea / 2057.

 - a87d: a 32-bit DWORD scroll-range denominator typed undefined2 (WORD) -> `a87d = 0x10000`
   truncated to 0 -> cef4 divide-by-zero (SIGFPE) on the first row-select.  -> uint32_t.

 - a8ee / a8f4 / a8f5: BYTE element dirty-masks (asm `mov BYTE PTR`) typed undefined2 (WORD) ->
   writing 3 clobbered the adjacent child-list head/link word -> the container child-walk found no
   children and the list never repainted on a selection change.  -> uint8_t.

 - FUN_0000_209e / FUN_0000_208a: the container child-walk read its base from the GLOBAL
   DAT_1000_fafe, which holds the MENU base (f7b8) while the modal dialog is up (the cursor redraw
   updates fafe) -> the repaint walked the wrong element list.  209e publishes the live walk base bp
   in the shim global g_fist_paintbp; 208a reads it (the asm uses the preserved bp register).

Shim: tools/native_main.c defines g_fist_ev_node + g_fist_paintbp (companions to g_fist_cf).

